    "q-143205": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143205",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =12$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=16,$ determine the smallest sample size required so that the standard error of the mean is less than $0.1.$",
      "worked_solution": "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nSince the population standard deviation is $\\sigma =\\sqrt{16}=4,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe require that the standard error is less than $0.1.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{n}} & <0.1 \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\frac{4}{0.1} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >40 \\\\ n & >{40}^{2} \\\\ n & >1\\,600.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest sample size is $n=1\\,601.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-143205-a",
